  "title": "Erdős Problem #1022",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Is there a constant $c_t$, where $c_t\\to \\infty$ as $t\\to \\infty$, such that if $\\mathcal{F}$ is a finite family of finite sets, all of size at least $t$, and for every set $X$ there are $<c_t\\lvert X\\rvert$ many $A\\in \\mathcal{F}$ with $A\\subseteq X$, then $\\mathcal{F}$ has chromatic number $2$ (in other words, has property B)?",
